.\" Process this file with
.\" groff -man -Tascii sgml2rtf.1
.\"
.TH SGML2RTF 1 "2025-04-06"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
sgml2rtf \- create RTF output from a LinuxDoc DTD SGML source file
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.B sgml2rtf [generic_option...] [--twosplit]
.IR file [.sgml]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.B sgml2rtf
is an old and obsoleted form of the rtf converter command
of LinuxDoc-Tools
(its name may be misleading, as it is not a tool for any SGML DTD, only
supports the SGML LinuxDoc DTD).
It is recommended to switch the new form
.B linuxdoc -B rtf
now.
It converts a LinuxDoc DTD SGML source file to RTF, the Rich Text Tormat
used by the Microsoft Windows help system.
Output will appear in the top level file
.I file.rtf
and
.I file-n.rtf
for each section, where
.I file
is the name of the SGML source file.
The RTF output is tailored for
compilation by the Windows Help Compiler (hc31.exe).
.LP
The attribute/value pair "output=rtf" is set for conditionals.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.B sgml2rtf
accepts all the generic options described in
.BR linuxdoc (1), and:
.IP "--twosplit, -2"
Splits files both at n. sections and n.m. subsections
.IP file
The SGML source file, named either
.I file
or
.I file.sgml
.SH "فایل‌ها (FILES)"
Many files and executables in /usr/share/linuxdoc-tools and /usr/bin are used.
.SH "اشکالات (BUGS)"
None known.
.SH "نویسنده (AUTHOR)"
Originally written by Steve Tynor <tynor@atlanta.twr.com>, and
Cees de Groot <cg@pobox.com> for sgml-tools (v1) and maintained by
Taketoshi Sano <sano@debian.org> for Linuxdoc-Tools.
Currently maintained by Agustin Martin <agustin6martin AT gmail com>.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.BR linuxdoc (1),
.BR sgml2html (1),
